
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
A,B,C are collinear [00]
CB = CA [01]
CD = CA [02]
B,E,D are collinear [03]
FC = FE [04]
FD = FC [05]
GE ∥ AB [06]
FG = FC [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. A,B,C are collinear [00] & AB ∥ EG [06] ⇒  ∠ECB = ∠CEG [08]
002. FC = FE [04] & FG = FC [07] & FD = FC [05] ⇒  G,C,E,D are concyclic [09]
003. G,C,E,D are concyclic [09] ⇒  ∠GCD = ∠GED [10]
004. CB = CA [01] & CD = CA [02] ⇒  CD = CB [11]
005. CD = CB [11] ⇒  ∠CDB = ∠DBC [12]
006. B,E,D are collinear [03] & A,B,C are collinear [00] & ∠GCD = ∠GED [10] & EG ∥ AB [06] & ∠CDB = ∠DBC [12] ⇒  ∠EBC = ∠CGE [13]
007. ∠ECB = ∠CEG [08] & ∠EBC = ∠CGE [13] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CB = EG
==========================
